  "method": [
    "Status matrix compares no acknowledgment, status register bit 31, and the dedicated PXCLK bit-12 clear strobe. Test-only status sampling runs through the existing interrupt worker at one-second intervals.",
    "Matched comparison uses exactly the same two-frame driver module in both emulators. Only experimental QEMU endpoint bulk-OUT pipelining differs. Both retain separate payload and zero-packet requests.",
    "Each matched trial requests 60 full-frame DIRTYFB updates/s for 20 seconds, with function profiling and usbmon enabled. CPU-load cases add a busy loop on the sole guest vCPU. These are diagnostic runs, not clean CPU comparisons.",
    "Steady-state statistics select the longest contiguous sequence of successful completions with the expected wire frame size and trim two seconds from each end. Rates use decimal MB/s.",
    "Frame-counter and LBUF measurements use status reply data from the same USB trace and measurement window. They do not depend on dmesg retention or add a second status reader.",
    "All performance variants predate the optional-DMA __GFP_NOWARN fix. The final production module was tested separately with panic_on_warn=1, default three-frame queue, and no periodic test sampler.",
    "Bulk completion errno -2 is ENOENT from deliberate modeset/restore cancellation. The production driver separately still logs Frame conversion failed: -2 during removal."
  ],
  "findings": [
    "The dedicated 0x8004 bit-12 strobe clears LBUF flags. Status bit 31 and writing observed bits 8/9 do not clear the observed overflow on this adapter. Blanked clear12 phases replace stale overflow with underflow; active streaming reasserts overflow in all modes.",
    "Matched normal QEMU delivers about 30 USB frames/s at synthetic 1080p60, while experimental pipelining delivers about 60/s for both formats, including guest CPU load. Controller frame count remains about 60/s. Emulator bulk-OUT serialization explains the measured rate halving.",
    "Overflow also appears with full-rate USB delivery, so its presence alone does not identify the rate-halving cause or establish visible glitches. LBUF fault recovery remains unimplemented.",
    "The production allocation warning came from direct DMA requesting order 11, beyond the tested kernel maximum order 10. __GFP_NOWARN suppresses expected optional allocation failure, preserving existing page fallback and IOMMU support."
  ],
